From cd4debc6828031c7760f07f45c8db4760983ca04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Witold=20Bo=C5=82t?= <witold.bolt@jit.team>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 22:50:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] plugins: add a memory plugin (Phoenix-RTOS)

A small panel item that shows how much physical memory is in use:
"Mem <used>/<total> GB" and a bar, green below 75 % used, yellow up
to 90 %, red above. Phoenix-RTOS has no OOM handling, so running out
of memory wedges the desktop with no warning; this makes it visible.

The figures come from Phoenix-RTOS meminfo(): one call every 2 s for
the totals. The kernel counts its file cache as free (it is given up
on demand), so "used" leaves it out; the cache and the largest free
block are not reported separately. The tooltip adds free memory and
the five processes with the most anonymous memory (threadsinfo() and
one meminfo() per process, done only while a tooltip is shown, at most
every 5 s, and for the log line).

At start, every 30 s and when the level goes up, one line goes to
/dev/console (stderr only if it cannot be opened):
  MEMMON t=<s> total_mb= used_mb= free_mb= cache_mb=- largest_kb=-
         top=<name>:<mb>,... all_mb= level=<green|yellow|red>

Built only for host_machine.system() == 'phoenix'; with
-Dbuiltin-plugins=true it is linked into the panel like the others.
BSD-3-Clause, new code.
